  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> be two ellipse whose centers are at the origin. The major axes of <math><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> lie along the x - axis and the y - axis, respectively. Let S be the circle <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The straight line <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> touches the curves&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> respectively. Suppose that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are the eccentricities of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math>respectively, then the correct expression(s) is(are)",
    "image": null
